# Lumenhold Academy — 简体中文 (zh-CN) translation of content/events/spotlight.grim
# Maintained by `node tools/grim.js i18n zh-CN`. Translate the text after "="; keep {tokens}.
# "# en:" shows the English source. [hash] marks the English version a line was translated from;
# lines marked STALE need updating — after fixing the text, delete the [hash] and re-run the tool.


@event renown_famous_entry
# en: Your Name in Every Mouth
title [b3b06c] = 人人口中的名字
# en: Somewhere this month it stopped being "have you heard of {player}" and became just "{player}". Corridors go quiet and then loud as you pass. The Ledger has stopped explaining who you are. You are, it seems, famous: the academy watches what you do now, and remembers.
text [62a380] = 这个月的某一天，人们不再说“你听说过{player}吗”，而是直接说“{player}”。你走过时，走廊先是一静，然后又热闹起来。《纪事报》已经不再解释你是谁。看来，你出名了：如今整个学院都在看你做什么，而且都记得。
# en: A crowded corridor parting around a student, heads turning in a wave, a first-year pointing and being shushed.
scene [f95646] = 拥挤的走廊在一个学生面前分开，一颗颗脑袋像波浪一样转过来，一个一年级生伸手去指，被人嘘了回去。
# en: Enjoy it
opt.left.label [8993d9] = 好好享受
# en: You let yourself enjoy it, for a week. The seats are better. The queues are shorter. Someone gives you the last slice of pudding without being asked. It is, you admit, very nice.
opt.left.say.1 [9dcedc] = 你允许自己享受了一个星期。座位更好了，队伍更短了，有人不等你开口就把最后一块布丁让给你。你承认，这感觉非常好。
# en: Keep your head down
opt.right.label [b59315] = 保持低调
# en: You keep to the library and the back row. It doesn't make much difference: people find you anyway. But you get a great deal of reading done, and they come away saying you're modest, which only makes it worse.
opt.right.say.1 [3e5e17] = 你待在图书馆和最后一排。这没什么用：人们照样找得到你。不过你读了很多书，而他们回去都说你很谦虚，这反倒更糟。

@event renown_legend_entry
# en: The Academy's Own Story
title [e990cd] = 学院自己的故事
# en: First-years tell stories about you that you don't recognise. A third-year swears you once did something you have never done, and the version where you did it is better. When you come into the Great Hall, it isn't quiet and it isn't loud: it simply watches. You've become part of what Lumenhold says about itself.
text [fbe263] = 一年级生讲着关于你的故事，你自己都认不出来。一个三年级生发誓说你做过一件你从没做过的事，而你做了的那个版本更精彩。你走进大礼堂时，那里既不安静也不喧闹：只是看着你。你已经成了流明堡讲述自己时的一部分。
# en: A great hall at supper, every head at every table turned toward one student coming in through the doors, as if a story had walked in.
scene [ef10af] = 晚餐时的大礼堂，每张桌子上的每一颗脑袋都转向刚从门口进来的一个学生，仿佛走进来的是一个故事。
# en: Live up to it
opt.left.label [4e38ae] = 不负其名
# en: You start getting up earlier, working later, being kinder in corridors, because people are watching and you'd like the story to be true. It mostly is. It's exhausting. It's worth it.
opt.left.say.1 [216c0c] = 你开始起得更早，睡得更晚，在走廊里待人更和气，因为人们在看，而你希望那些故事是真的。大部分确实是。这很累人。也很值得。
# en: Correct the stories
opt.right.label [ea70ff] = 纠正那些故事
# en: You start telling people, cheerfully, which bits never happened. It makes no difference whatever to the stories. It makes a great deal of difference to the people who hear you say it.
opt.right.say.1 [b42bce] = 你开始高高兴兴地告诉别人，哪些部分从没发生过。这对故事本身毫无影响。对听你这么说的人，影响却很大。

@event spot_ledger_profile
# en: A Profile in the Ledger
title [5e7e90] = 《纪事报》人物专访
# en: Nessa wants you for the Ledger: a whole column, "Who Is {player}?", with an interview. Her quill is already hovering. "Tell me everything," she says. "Or tell me something better than everything. Readers can't tell the difference. I can."
text [3e4f3f] = 内莎想让你上《纪事报》：整整一栏，《{player}是谁？》，还要专访。她的羽毛笔已经悬在半空。“全告诉我，”她说，“或者告诉我比全部更精彩的东西。读者分不出来。我分得出来。”
# en: A cluttered newspaper office, an editor with a self-writing quill hovering over a notebook, a student in the visitor's chair looking uneasy.
scene [3ac32d] = 杂乱的报社办公室里，一位编辑的自动羽毛笔悬在笔记本上方，来访者椅子上的学生显得有些不安。
# en: Be candid
opt.left.label [af726f] = 实话实说
# en: You tell her the truth, including the dull parts and one embarrassing one. The column is warm and true and a little bit unflattering. People like you more for it. You wish they'd stop quoting the embarrassing part.
opt.left.say.1 [bb5e93] = 你把真话告诉了她，包括无聊的部分和一件丢脸的事。那篇专栏温暖、真实，还有一点不那么体面。人们因此更喜欢你了。你只希望他们别再引用那件丢脸的事。
# en: Polish the story
opt.right.label [b04a62] = 润色一下
# en: You give her a better version of yourself: braver, wittier, slightly taller. Nessa writes it all down with a look you can't read. The column is a sensation. Some of it is even true.
opt.right.say.1 [d8e4c5] = 你给了她一个更好的你：更勇敢，更机智，还稍微高一点。内莎全记了下来，神情让你捉摸不透。专栏轰动一时。其中有些甚至是真的。
# en: Nessa stops writing halfway through the story about the dragon. "There was no dragon," she says. The column runs anyway, short and faintly amused. "We checked," it says, twice.
opt.right.say.2 [dbd49e] = 你讲到那条龙的时候，内莎停了笔。“根本没有龙，”她说。专栏照样登了，短短一篇，带着淡淡的笑意。“我们核实过了，”文中写道，写了两遍。

@event spot_judge_exhibition
# en: A Judge for the First-Years
title [1ac9e2] = 一年级的评委
# en: The first-years' duelling exhibition needs a judge, and they've asked for you by name. Twelve bouts, a scorecard, a little brass bell. Every first-year in the hall wants to impress you. Every one of their friends is in the gallery.
text [0cae44] = 一年级的决斗表演赛需要一位评委，他们点名要你。十二场比试，一张记分卡，一只小铜铃。场上每个一年级生都想给你留下好印象。他们的每一个朋友都坐在看台上。
# en: A duelling floor ringed by nervous first-years in practice robes, a student at a small table with a scorecard and a bell.
scene [05425b] = 决斗场地四周围着穿练习袍的紧张一年级生，一个学生坐在小桌后，面前放着记分卡和一只铃。
# en: Judge it strictly
opt.left.label [2a93bd] = 严格评判
# en: You score every bout to the rules, including the one where the favourite lost on a foot fault. The gallery boos. The first-year who won on the foot fault looks at you as if you'd hung the moon.
opt.left.say.1 [298d53] = 你每一场都按规则打分，包括热门选手因为脚步犯规而输掉的那场。看台上一片嘘声。靠对方脚步犯规赢下来的那个一年级生看着你，就像你为TA摘下了月亮。
# en: Play to the crowd
opt.right.label [fc1a82] = 迎合观众
# en: You ring the bell with a flourish, give a speech between bouts, and somehow every first-year comes away with a prize for something. The hall loves it. Two of the duellists who deserved to win know they were robbed.
opt.right.say.1 [e6b54b] = 你花哨地摇铃，在比试之间发表演说，结果每个一年级生都因为某件事拿了奖。全场都爱死了。两个本该获胜的决斗者知道自己被抢了。

@event spot_village_recognised
# en: Is It You?
title [606872] = 是你吗？
# en: In the village, a baker leans out of the window and says, "It's you, isn't it? From the Ledger?" By the time you've said yes, there are children, a dog, and an old man who wants to tell you what the academy was like in his day.
text [efb1c8] = 在村子里，一个面包师从窗口探出身来说：“是你吧？《纪事报》上那个？”等你说完“是”，身边已经围了一群孩子、一条狗，还有一位老人，想告诉你他那个年代的学院是什么样子。
# en: A village square, a baker leaning out of a shop window with a tray of buns, children gathering round a student in academy robes.
scene [03c34d] = 村子的广场上，面包师端着一盘小圆面包从店窗里探出身，孩子们围着一个穿学院长袍的学生。
# en: Stay and talk
opt.left.label [430859] = 留下来聊聊
# en: You stay the afternoon. You eat a free bun, admire the dog, and hear three versions of the old man's story. You walk back up the hill much later than you meant to, with flour on your sleeve.
opt.left.say.1 [465f8b] = 你待了一下午。吃了一个免费的面包，夸了那条狗，听了老人的故事的三个版本。你走回山上时比原打算晚了很多，袖子上沾着面粉。
# en: Smile and slip away
opt.right.label [1eb8d6] = 笑一笑，悄悄溜走
# en: You thank the baker, buy a bun like anyone else, and slip away before the crowd thickens. Behind you, the old man is telling the story to the dog.
opt.right.say.1 [205b2f] = 你谢过面包师，像别人一样买了个面包，在人群变多之前溜走了。身后，那位老人正把故事讲给那条狗听。

@event spot_fan_charm
# en: A Charm From a Stranger
title [0059fc] = 陌生人的护身符
# en: A first-year you've never spoken to waits outside your lecture to give you a charm: a little knot of blue thread on a ribbon, clearly made by hand, clearly not very well. "For luck," the first-year says, to the floor. "I made it. You don't have to wear it."
text [41e307] = 一个你从没说过话的一年级生在讲堂外等你，要送你一个护身符：一小团蓝线打的结，系在缎带上，一看就是手工做的，一看就做得不太好。“保佑你的，”那个一年级生对着地板说，“我自己做的。你不用戴。”
# en: A first-year holding out a small knotted charm on a ribbon at arm's length, looking at the floor, an older student bending to take it.
scene [540def] = 一个一年级生伸直手臂递出一个系在缎带上的小绳结护身符，眼睛盯着地面，一个年长的学生弯腰去接。
# en: Wear it where people can see
opt.left.label [ab1b6e] = 戴在显眼的地方
# en: You tie it to your bag strap. Within a week every first-year in the castle is knotting blue thread, and the one who made yours walks past you every morning, very straight, very proud.
opt.left.say.1 [37a54b] = 你把它系在书包带上。一个星期之内，城堡里每个一年级生都在打蓝线结，而给你做护身符的那个，每天早上从你身边走过，腰板挺得笔直，骄傲极了。
# en: Thank them, and keep it in a pocket
opt.right.label [d25df8] = 道谢，放进口袋
# en: "I'll keep it close," you say, and you do, in the inside pocket nobody sees. The first-year goes pink and runs. It's still there at the end of the year, a little frayed.
opt.right.say.1 [a8acb6] = “我会贴身带着，”你说，你也确实这么做了，放在谁也看不见的内袋里。那个一年级生脸一红，跑开了。到学年结束时它还在那儿，有点磨毛了。

@event spot_signature
# en: Sign This?
title [5957f5] = 能签个名吗？
# en: A first-year has their warding textbook open at the chapter on circles, and a quill held out. "Could you sign it? Next to the diagram. Everyone says you got it in your first week."
text [96ef47] = 一个一年级生把结界课本翻到讲法阵的那一章，递过来一支羽毛笔。“能签个名吗？签在图旁边。大家都说你第一周就弄懂了。”
# en: A library corridor, a younger student holding out an open textbook and a quill, an older student hesitating over the page.
scene [e5e7c1] = 图书馆的走廊里，一个年轻学生递出一本摊开的课本和一支羽毛笔，一个年长的学生对着书页犹豫。
# en: Sign it with a flourish
opt.left.label [f423ec] = 潇洒地签上
# en: You sign it, with a little drawn circle for good measure. The textbook goes round the first-year dormitory by supper. By the end of the week three more appear, and a library book, which you decline.
opt.left.say.1 [585d3b] = 你签了，还顺手画了个小法阵。晚饭前，这本课本已经在一年级宿舍里传了一圈。到周末，又冒出来三本，还有一本图书馆的书，你婉拒了。
# en: Show them the rune instead
opt.right.label [1973a5] = 教他们画法阵
# en: You don't sign it. You take the quill and draw the circle properly in the margin, slowly, and make the first-year draw it back. "There. Now it's yours." The first-year looks disappointed, and then, by the third try, astonished.
opt.right.say.1 [c29111] = 你没有签名。你接过羽毛笔，在页边慢慢地把法阵好好画了一遍，再让那个一年级生照着画回来。“好了。现在它是你的了。”那个一年级生先是失望，到第三次时，变成了惊讶。

@event spot_house_speech
# en: A Few Words
title [13224b] = 说几句
# en: At the end-of-term supper, a final-year at the top of your table taps a glass and says that {player}, who has done the table such credit this term, will now say a few words. Nobody told you about the few words. The whole table turns.
text [3bed86] = 学期末的晚宴上，坐在你们这桌上首的一个毕业班学生敲了敲杯子，宣布这学期为全桌争了光的{player}现在要讲几句话。没人跟你提过要讲几句话。整张桌子都转了过来。
# en: A long table at supper, candles lit, a student halfway to their feet with a cup in hand, every face along the table turned their way.
scene [161380] = 晚餐时点着蜡烛的长桌边，一个学生手握杯子，刚站起一半，桌边每一张脸都朝着这个学生。
# en: Make a speech
opt.left.label [520c02] = 发表演讲
# en: You say something short and true about the people at this table, and sit down before you can spoil it. They bang the table for you. A third-year you barely know shakes your hand after, hard.
opt.left.say.1 [46f7a3] = 你简短而真诚地讲了讲这张桌子边的人，在自己搞砸之前坐了下来。他们为你拍桌子。一个你几乎不认识的三年级生事后用力握了握你的手。
# en: You start well and lose the thread somewhere around "and in conclusion". Your table cheers anyway, loyally and a bit too loudly. You eat your pudding very fast.
opt.left.say.2 [f0ae47] = 你开头不错，到“总而言之”那里就乱了。全桌照样为你欢呼，忠诚而且有点太响了。你飞快地吃完了布丁。
# en: Raise your cup and sit
opt.right.label [93b50b] = 举杯，坐下
# en: You raise your cup, say "to all of you", and sit down. It turns out that's all anybody wanted. The table drinks, and goes back to arguing about the pudding.
opt.right.say.1 [4b2956] = 你举起杯子，说了句“敬大家”，就坐下了。原来大家要的也就是这个。全桌喝了一口，又回去争论布丁了。

@event spot_resentful
# en: All Anyone Talks About
title [831bec] = 大家都在谈论你
# en: {o} has been short with you all week. Tonight, when the common room gathers round you for the third time to hear about something you did, {o} shuts {o.their} book hard and says, to nobody, "Some of us did things this term too."
text [f548a8] = {o}这一个星期对你都很冷淡。今晚，公共休息室里的人第三次围过来听你讲你做过的事时，{o}啪地合上书，对着空气说：“这学期别人也做了些事。”
# en: A common room, a student sitting stiffly apart with a book they're not reading, glancing at a crowd gathered around someone else.
scene [35622c] = 公共休息室里，一个学生僵硬地坐在一旁，手里的书并没有在读，瞥着围在另一个人身边的人群。
# en: Turn the room to {o}
opt.left.label [df07a8] = 把大家的目光转向{o}
# en: "{o} did, actually," you say, and tell them about it, the thing {o} did that nobody noticed. The room turns. {o} goes red, and then, slowly, starts telling it properly. Later {o} says thank you, gruffly.
opt.left.say.1 [b1ccd0] = “{o}确实做了，”你说，然后讲起那件事，{o}做的、没人注意到的那件事。大家转过身来。{o}脸红了，然后，慢慢地，开始亲自好好讲起来。后来，{o}粗声粗气地向你道了谢。
# en: Let it pass
opt.right.label [7680ac] = 随它去
# en: You let it pass, and the room moves on, back to you. {o} goes up to bed early. It sits between you for a while, like a coat on a chair nobody will move.
opt.right.say.1 [9c005f] = 你没有接话，房间里的话题又回到了你身上。{o}早早上楼睡觉去了。这件事在你们之间搁了一阵子，像一件没人肯挪开的、搭在椅子上的外套。

@event spot_letters_page
# en: Letters to the Editor
title [69e221] = 读者来信
# en: The Ledger's letters page is about you this week. "Sir, I write to complain about {player}'s conduct in the library," says one. "Sir, I write to defend {player}, who is a credit to us all," says another, in what is very clearly the same handwriting. Half the castle is reading it.
text [5b7211] = 这周《纪事报》的读者来信版全是关于你的。“先生，我写信投诉{player}在图书馆里的行为，”一封信写道。“先生，我写信为{player}辩护，此人是我们所有人的骄傲，”另一封写道，笔迹明显出自同一人之手。半个城堡都在读。
# en: A newspaper's letters page pinned to a corridor board, students crowding round to read it, one of them laughing behind their hand.
scene [6c5017] = 走廊的布告板上钉着一张报纸的读者来信版，学生们挤着看，其中一个用手捂着嘴偷笑。
# en: Write in yourself
opt.left.label [83fa80] = 亲自写信
# en: You write a short, grave letter apologising for your conduct in the library, which you say was "a sneeze of uncommon violence". It runs on the front page. The library gives you a round of applause.
opt.left.say.1 [f73536] = 你写了一封简短而郑重的信，为自己在图书馆里的行为道歉，说那是“一个异常猛烈的喷嚏”。它登上了头版。图书馆为你鼓了掌。
# en: Your letter tries to be funny and comes out pompous. The next issue has three letters about your letter. You resolve never to write to a newspaper again.
opt.left.say.2 [b5b52e] = 你的信想写得有趣，结果写得自命不凡。下一期刊登了三封关于你那封信的信。你下定决心再也不给报纸写信。
# en: Ignore it entirely
opt.right.label [f9d712] = 完全不理
# en: You don't read it, which is harder than it sounds when everyone keeps reading it to you. By the next week there's a new scandal: someone has been taking two puddings. You are forgotten, gratefully.
opt.right.say.1 [9f0046] = 你没有去读，这比听起来难，因为每个人都不停地念给你听。到下周，有了新的丑闻：有人一直在拿两份布丁。你被遗忘了，谢天谢地。

@event spot_saved_seats
# en: The Seat Problem
title [4889a6] = 座位问题
# en: {~Three different tables have saved you a seat at lunch, and all three are waving.|You can't sit down in the refectory any more without someone having saved the spot "for you", whether you wanted it or not.|Somebody you have never met has saved you a seat, and is offended you haven't taken it.} Your own friends are at the corner table, where they always are, watching to see where you'll go.
text [8932a7] = {~午饭时有三张不同的桌子给你留了座位，三张桌子都在冲你招手。|如今你在膳堂里一坐下，总有人已经“为你”占好了位置，不管你想不想要。|一个你从没见过的人给你留了座位，而你没坐过去，对方很生气。}你自己的朋友坐在角落那张桌子，他们一向坐在那儿，正看着你会往哪儿走。
# en: A refectory at lunch, three different tables each with a student waving at an empty seat, a fourth student standing in the middle with a tray.
scene [6538ef] = 午饭时的膳堂，三张不同的桌子上各有一个学生朝空座招手，第四个学生端着托盘站在中间。
# en: Sit with your friends
opt.left.label [b55f91] = 和朋友坐
# en: {~You walk past all three waving tables to the corner. Your friends make a great show of not caring, and then shift up to make room.|You sit where you always sit. One table looks hurt. Your friends look smug.|You sit down at the corner. "Oh, we're good enough for you, are we?" says someone, delighted.}
opt.left.say.1 [e33c07] = {~你从三张招手的桌子旁走过，去了角落。你的朋友们装作毫不在意，然后挪了挪给你腾出位置。|你坐在老地方。一张桌子显得很受伤。你的朋友们显得很得意。|你在角落坐下。“哦，我们配得上你啦？”有人说，高兴得很。}
# en: Take a saved seat
opt.right.label [1bcba7] = 坐留好的座位
# en: {~You sit at the nearest table and are asked forty questions. It's flattering. At the corner table, your friends are laughing at something without you.|You take the saved seat, and the table is very kind, and you can't remember any of their names afterwards.|You sit with the stranger, who is thrilled, and tells you about their aunt. Your friends wave from across the hall.}
opt.right.say.1 [d5867d] = {~你在最近的桌子坐下，被问了四十个问题。这很让人受用。角落那张桌子上，你的朋友们正为什么事笑着，没有你。|你坐到留好的座位上，那桌人都很和善，可事后你一个名字都记不起来。|你和那个陌生人坐在一起，对方激动极了，跟你讲起自己的姨妈。你的朋友们在大厅那头朝你挥手。}

@event spot_shop_window
# en: The Window Table
title [b8283c] = 靠窗的桌子
# en: A tearoom in the village has noticed that when you sit in its window, people come in. The owner makes you an offer: your tea is free, for the rest of the term, so long as you drink it in the window, where it can be seen.
text [3762e6] = 村里一家茶室发现，只要你坐在它的窗边，就会有人进来。店主给你开了个条件：这学期剩下的日子里你的茶免费，只要你坐在窗边喝，让人看得见。
# en: A village tearoom window with a reserved card on its best table, a shopkeeper beckoning a student in from the street.
scene [a1823b] = 村里一家茶室的窗口，最好的那张桌子上摆着“已预订”的卡片，店主正招手把街上的一个学生请进来。
# en: Take the window
opt.left.label [8ae02b] = 坐到窗边
# en: You drink a great deal of free tea in the window, smiling at strangers who press their noses to the glass. The tearoom is full every afternoon. You can never quite read your book.
opt.left.say.1 [c27556] = 你在窗边喝了很多免费的茶，对着把鼻子贴在玻璃上的陌生人微笑。茶室每天下午都坐满了人。你的书却总也读不进去。
# en: Pay for your tea
opt.right.label [d38fb7] = 自己付茶钱
# en: You thank the owner and pay, and sit at the back, where nobody sees you. You read four chapters in peace. The owner, a little put out, brings you extra biscuits anyway.
opt.right.say.1 [e663b3] = 你谢过店主，付了钱，坐到后面没人看得见的地方。你安安静静地读了四章。店主有点不痛快，还是给你多送了几块饼干。

@event spot_impression
# en: Somebody Doing You
title [601669] = 有人在演你
# en: At the end-of-term skits in the common room, a second-year gets up on a chair and does you. The walk, the face you make in lectures, the thing you say when you lose at cards. It is very, very accurate. The whole room is looking at you to see how you'll take it.
text [2fb3c9] = 学期末公共休息室里的小品会上，一个二年级生站到椅子上，开始学你。走路的样子，上课时的表情，打牌输了时说的那句话。非常、非常像。整个房间都在看你，看你会是什么反应。
# en: An end-of-term skit in a common room, a student on a chair doing an exaggerated impression, the room in stitches, one student in the audience watching their own walk being copied.
scene [43a472] = 学期末公共休息室里的小品表演，一个学生站在椅子上夸张地模仿，满屋子的人笑得前仰后合，观众里有一个学生正看着自己的走路姿势被人学去。
# en: Get up and do them back
opt.left.label [572a07] = 上去学回来
# en: You climb up on the next chair and do them doing you. The room goes wild. The second-year laughs so hard they fall off the chair. It becomes, for a term, a double act.
opt.left.say.1 [2ee4c9] = 你爬上旁边的椅子，学起了那个学你的人。全场沸腾了。那个二年级生笑得从椅子上掉了下来。这一学期，你们成了一对搭档。
# en: You climb up, and freeze, and the second-year does you freezing, which gets the biggest laugh of the night. You laugh too, eventually. It takes a while.
opt.left.say.2 [f4e647] = 你爬了上去，然后僵住了，那个二年级生又学起你僵住的样子，赢得了当晚最大的笑声。最后你也笑了。花了好一会儿。
# en: Laugh along
opt.right.label [ccfaef] = 跟着笑
# en: You laugh, properly, because it is funny. The second-year bows to you at the end. You notice, for the rest of the week, that you've stopped making the face in lectures.
opt.right.say.1 [83a10d] = 你笑了，真心实意地笑，因为确实好笑。结束时那个二年级生向你鞠了一躬。那个星期剩下的日子里，你发现自己上课时不再做那个表情了。

@event spot_name_dropped
# en: A Friend of {player}'s
title [b4acce] = {player}的朋友
# en: You come round a corner and hear {o} telling a little crowd of second-years that {o.they} and {player} are "very close, actually", and that you "always ask {o.their} advice". You've spoken to {o} perhaps four times. {o} turns, and sees you.
text [b7e40d] = 你拐过一个弯，听见{o}正在对一小群二年级生说，{o.they}和{player}“其实很熟”，说你“总是来问{o.their}意见”。你和{o}大概只说过四次话。{o}转过身，看见了你。
# en: A student talking grandly to a group of younger students in a corridor, an arm flung out, the person they're talking about rounding the corner behind them.
scene [7b9679] = 走廊里一个学生正挥着手臂对一群年轻学生高谈阔论，他们谈论的那个人正从身后的拐角走过来。
# en: Play along
opt.left.label [55ddb6] = 顺着说
# en: "We are," you say. "Terrible advice, mostly." The second-years laugh. {o} looks at you with such gratitude that you find, over the next month, that you do start asking {o.their} advice. Some of it is quite good.
opt.left.say.1 [092de5] = “是啊，”你说，“大多是馊主意。”二年级生们笑了。{o}满怀感激地看着你，结果接下来一个月里，你发现自己真的开始问{o.their}意见了。有些还挺不错。
# en: Set it straight, kindly
opt.right.label [d6c817] = 委婉地澄清
# en: "We've met," you say pleasantly, "a few times." {o} goes scarlet. The second-years drift away. {o} avoids you for a while, and then, one day, sits down and talks to you properly, about nothing much.
opt.right.say.1 [9c97ed] = “我们见过，”你和气地说，“几次。”{o}的脸一下子红透了。二年级生们散开了。{o}躲了你一阵子，后来有一天，坐下来和你好好聊了聊，聊的都是些无关紧要的事。

@event spot_professor_example
# en: As {player} Showed Us
title [fa8598] = 正如{player}向我们展示的
# en: In the middle of a lecture, the lecturer says, "As {player} showed us last week," and describes something you did, slightly wrong, as the right way to do it. Forty heads turn. You know, and you're fairly sure the lecturer doesn't, that it only worked by accident.
text [d2a212] = 讲课讲到一半，讲师说：“正如{player}上周向我们展示的，”然后描述了你做过的一件事，描述得略有偏差，还把它当成了正确做法。四十颗脑袋转了过来。你知道，而且你很确定讲师不知道，那次能成功纯属意外。
# en: A lecture hall, a professor gesturing toward one student in the third row, the rest of the class turning to look.
scene [b50de0] = 阶梯教室里，一位教授朝第三排的一个学生比画，全班都转过头去看。
# en: Say it was an accident
opt.left.label [80edf4] = 说那是意外
# en: You put your hand up and say it was mostly luck. The lecturer looks at you for a long moment, then laughs, and makes the class work out why it shouldn't have worked. It's the best lecture of the term.
opt.left.say.1 [b20958] = 你举手说那主要是运气。讲师看了你好一会儿，然后笑了，让全班推算为什么那本不该成功。那是这学期最好的一堂课。
# en: Let it stand
opt.right.label [d81aa7] = 就让它这样
# en: You say nothing. The class writes it down. For the rest of the term people ask you to show them how, and you have to work out, in secret and in a hurry, how you did it.
opt.right.say.1 [cd3b1c] = 你什么也没说。全班都记了下来。那学期剩下的日子里，人们一直请你演示怎么做，你只好偷偷地、匆匆忙忙地弄明白自己当初是怎么做到的。

@event spot_three_invitations
# en: Three Invitations, One Evening
title [c19b7d] = 一个晚上，三份邀请
# en: Three invitations for the same evening: a supper at the Gilded Newt with people who matter, a stargazing party on the observatory roof, and your oldest friend here, who just wants to play cards in the common room like you used to.
text [c64f9f] = 同一个晚上来了三份邀请：在镀金蝾螈酒馆和要紧人物共进晚餐，在观星台楼顶参加观星派对，还有你在这里最老的朋友，只想像从前那样在公共休息室里打牌。
# en: A student at a desk with three different invitation cards fanned out in one hand, a calendar with one evening circled three times.
scene [38c342] = 一个学生坐在书桌前，一只手里扇形展开三张不同的请柬，日历上同一个晚上被圈了三次。
# en: Go where you'll be seen
opt.left.label [e96d78] = 去会被人看见的地方
# en: The Newt supper is loud and full of people who know your name. You make three useful acquaintances and laugh a great deal. Walking back, you think of the card game, and wonder who won.
opt.left.say.1 [9f1c52] = 蝾螈酒馆的晚宴热闹非凡，满座都是知道你名字的人。你结识了三位有用的人，笑了很多。走回去的路上，你想起那场牌局，不知道最后是谁赢了。
# en: Play cards with your friend
opt.right.label [b6cf49] = 和朋友打牌
# en: You send two polite notes and go down to the common room. Your friend looks up, surprised, and deals you in without a word. You lose every hand. It's the best evening of the month.
opt.right.say.1 [3ff48d] = 你写了两张客气的便条，下楼去了公共休息室。你的朋友抬起头，有些意外，一言不发地给你发了牌。你每一把都输了。那是这个月最好的一个晚上。

@event spot_family_tour
# en: Show Them Round
title [164e2a] = 带他们转转
# en: A note comes down from the Headmistress's Tower: a family is visiting, their eldest starts next autumn, and they've asked, having read about you, whether you might show them round. The eldest is pale with nerves. The parents have a list of questions. The youngest wants to see a dragon.
text [0180d6] = 院长塔送来一张便条：有一家人来参观，他们的长子明年秋天入学，因为在报上读到过你，问你能不能带他们四处看看。那位长子紧张得脸色发白。父母列了一张问题清单。最小的孩子想看龙。
# en: A student leading a nervous family through a castle courtyard, a small child staring up at the towers, a parent clutching a prospectus.
scene [f2f421] = 一个学生领着一家紧张的人穿过城堡庭院，一个小孩仰头盯着塔楼，一位家长紧紧攥着一本招生简章。
# en: Show them the polished academy
opt.left.label [c5c519] = 带他们看光鲜的学院
# en: You take them the long way: the Great Hall at its brightest, the library from the good end, the observatory with the sun on it. You skip the draughty stairs and the lecture with the smell. The parents are dazzled. The eldest looks more frightened than ever.
opt.left.say.1 [76a581] = 你带他们绕了远路：最明亮时的大礼堂，从好的那头看过去的图书馆，洒满阳光的观星台。你跳过了漏风的楼梯和那间有怪味的教室。父母看得眼花缭乱。那位长子看上去比之前更害怕了。
# en: Show them the real one
opt.right.label [d7f3af] = 带他们看真实的学院
# en: You show them the draughty stairs, the bench where everyone cries before exams, and the kitchen door where the kind cook leaves buns. The parents look a little doubtful. The eldest, for the first time, smiles. "So people get lost here too?" Constantly, you tell them.
opt.right.say.1 [221580] = 你带他们看了漏风的楼梯，看了大家考试前都会在上面哭的那条长凳，还有厨房后门，好心的厨子会在那儿留面包。父母显得有点将信将疑。那位长子第一次露出了笑容。“这么说，在这儿也会迷路？”你告诉他们，经常。

@event spot_owl_mail
# en: Letters From Strangers
title [6abfcd] = 陌生人的来信
# en: {~The owls have started bringing you letters from people you've never met: a farmer's child who wants to come to Lumenhold, a retired professor with opinions, someone who wants to know if you're single.|There are eleven letters on your windowsill this morning, and an owl asleep on top of them, looking put-upon.|Another heap of letters from strangers. One has a pressed flower in it. One is just a drawing of you, with very large hands.}
text [aa47fe] = {~猫头鹰开始给你送来陌生人的信：一个想来流明堡的农家孩子，一位很有主见的退休教授，还有人想知道你是不是单身。|今天早上你的窗台上有十一封信，上面还睡着一只猫头鹰，一副受了委屈的样子。|又是一堆陌生人的来信。一封里夹着一朵压干的花。一封只是一幅你的画像，手画得特别大。}
# en: A dormitory windowsill heaped with letters, a tired delivery owl sitting on the pile, a student reading one with a candle.
scene [1e289c] = 宿舍的窗台上堆满了信，一只疲惫的送信猫头鹰坐在信堆上，一个学生借着烛光读其中一封。
# en: Answer every one
opt.left.label [6e5098] = 每一封都回
# en: {~You spend the evening writing back, one after another, until your hand aches. The farmer's child writes again within a week, in very careful capitals.|You answer every letter, even the one with the drawing, and thank its artist for the hands.|It takes two evenings. You sleep badly and dream of owls. Somewhere out there, eleven people are very pleased.}
opt.left.say.1 [875a10] = {~你花了一整个晚上一封接一封地回信，直到手发酸。不到一个星期，那个农家孩子又写来了信，用非常认真的大写字母。|你回了每一封信，连那幅画像也回了，还感谢画家把你的手画得那么大。|这花了两个晚上。你睡得不好，梦里全是猫头鹰。在外面的某个地方，有十一个人非常高兴。}
# en: Keep them, answer none
opt.right.label [8a30b2] = 收好，一封也不回
# en: {~You put them in a box under the bed and get on with your reading. Now and then you take one out and read it again. You never quite manage to write back.|The box under the bed is getting full. The owl gives you a long, reproachful look on its way out.|You read them all, at least. The pressed flower goes in a book. You mean to answer that one. You don't.}
opt.right.say.1 [6dfe02] = {~你把它们放进床底下的一只盒子里，接着读书。偶尔你会拿出一封再读一遍。你始终没能回信。|床底下的盒子越来越满了。猫头鹰临走时责备地看了你很久。|至少你每一封都读了。那朵压干的花夹进了一本书里。你本想回那一封的。你没有。}

@event spot_notes_for_sale
# en: Your Notes, For Sale
title [17637d] = 你的笔记，出售中
# en: Somebody has been copying your lecture notes and selling them in the common room as "the {player} method", a few coppers a copy, and there's a queue. The seller, a cheerful third-year with a cash tin, sees you and doesn't even look guilty. "You could have a cut," they offer.
text [1e2999] = 有人一直在抄你的课堂笔记，在公共休息室里当作“{player}学习法”出售，几个铜板一份，还排起了队。卖家是个乐呵呵的三年级生，捧着一只钱匣，看见你，连一点心虚的样子都没有。“你可以分一成，”对方提议。
# en: A common room table covered in copied pages, a student with a cash tin selling sheaves of notes, a queue of younger students waiting.
scene [d4fa06] = 公共休息室的桌子上铺满了抄写的纸页，一个学生捧着钱匣在卖一沓沓笔记，一群年纪小的学生排着队。
# en: Take a cut
opt.left.label [7b3269] = 分一成
# en: You take your cut and correct a few pages so the copies are at least right. The money is very welcome. A first-year thanks you, earnestly, for the notes they paid for. It sits a little wrong with you all week.
opt.left.say.1 [e36007] = 你拿了你那一份，还改正了几页，好让抄本至少是对的。这笔钱来得正是时候。一个一年级生诚恳地感谢你，为了那份花钱买来的笔记。这一整个星期，你心里都有点不是滋味。
# en: Give them away free
opt.right.label [4ac3ee] = 免费送出去
# en: You buy the last copy yourself and pin it to the common-room board, free to anyone. The seller sighs and closes the tin. By supper there's a queue at the board instead, and someone has added a note at the bottom: "thank you".
opt.right.say.1 [4f94ca] = 你自己买下最后一份，钉在公共休息室的布告板上，谁都可以看。卖家叹了口气，合上了钱匣。到晚饭时，排队的人换到了布告板前，有人在最下面添了一行字：“谢谢”。
